/**
@defgroup server Server
@brief Startup, listeners, TLS handshake and ALPN dispatch.

The program entry point parses the command line (parse_command_line()) and runs ServerApp,
which builds the shared Botan::TLS::Context (create_tls_context()) and starts
one run_tcp_listener() per port. Each accepted socket goes to a
TlsSessionHandler, which performs the TLS handshake with a
ServerStreamCallbacks and passes the stream to the IProtocolHandler that
matches the negotiated ALPN protocol.

@dot
digraph connection {
   rankdir=LR;
   node [shape=box, fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=10];
   edge [fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=9];
   TcpListener [label="run_tcp_listener"];
   TlsSessionHandler -> Http2ProtocolHandler [label="ALPN h2"];
   TlsSessionHandler -> WebSocketProtocolHandler [label="ALPN http/1.1"];
   TcpListener -> TlsSessionHandler;
   Http2ProtocolHandler -> H2ConnectionRunner -> H2Session -> WebApplication;
   WebSocketProtocolHandler -> serve_websocket -> pump_seconds_counter;
}
@enddot

The HTTPS port serves both protocols, so a browser reaches the page and
wss://host:port/ws with the same certificate exception. The --ws-port
listener always serves the WebSocket and exists for clients that are not
a browser.

@defgroup tls TLS
@brief Botan callbacks, credentials, policy and the connection details reported to the page.

ServerStreamCallbacks is created per connection. It selects the ALPN
protocol (select_alpn_protocol()), staples the OCSP response and records
the negotiated key exchange group, which ApiHandler later reports as JSON
(to_json()). BasicCredentialsManager and load_tls_policy() feed the shared
TLS context.

@defgroup http HTTP
@brief Application layer: routing, REST API and static files.

Independent of nghttp2: handlers receive an H2Request and answer through an
IH2Responder. WebApplication routes /api to ApiHandler and everything else
to StaticFileHandler.

@defgroup h2 HTTP/2
@ingroup http
@brief Server-side HTTP/2 on top of nghttp2, split into protocol engine and I/O loop.

H2Session (an IH2Engine) turns bytes into requests and responses into bytes
and never touches a socket. H2ConnectionRunner moves bytes between the
engine and an Asio stream and enforces the idle timeout. There is no
HTTP/1.1 fallback, no h2c upgrade and no extended CONNECT.

@defgroup ws WebSocket
@brief RFC 6455 over an established TLS stream, with a seconds counter as demo service.

serve_websocket() reads the HTTP/1.1 upgrade request, answers 101 and runs
pump_seconds_counter(). Frames are parsed by FrameParser and written with
write_frame(). The coroutines are templates on the stream type and work on
a plain socket as well as on Botan::TLS::Stream.

@defgroup ocsp OCSP
@brief Fetching and caching of OCSP responses for stapling.

OcspCache is the IOcspProvider used by the TLS callbacks. On a miss it
fetches through BeastOcspFetcher (HTTP/1.1 POST with Boost.Beast), checks
the status and keeps the response in OcspResponseStore for the time given by
estimate_cache_duration().

@defgroup common Common
@brief Logging, clock, error classification and string helpers.
*/
